==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|androgyne}}, from {{der|en|la|androgynus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæn.dɹə.d͡ʒaɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-androgyne.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who is [[androgynous]]. {{defdate|from mid-16th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1969|author=Kurt Vonnegut|title=Slaughterhouse-Five
|passage=Billy looked up at the face that went with the clogs. It was the face of a blond angel, of a fifteen-year-old boy. The boy was as beautiful as Eve. Billy was helped to his feet by the lovely boy, by the heavenly '''androgyne'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1981|author=w:William Irwin Thompson|title=The Time Falling Bodies Take to Light: Mythology, Sexuality and the Origins of Culture|publisher=Rider/Hutchinson & Co.|location=London|page=33|passage=The yogi is in this way the '''androgyne''' of prehistory reachieved.}}
# An [[androgynous]] [[plant]].

